+## Routes
+
+- `POST /import/sales`: accepts `{ "csv": "ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty\n..." }`.
+  Each row sells `qty` positive whole portions of the dish's recipe. `soldAt`
+  must be an ISO instant with a timezone. Returns `{ "tickets": 2, "dishes": 5 }`:
+  the number of newly imported tickets and total dish portions. Previously
+  imported tickets are skipped in full. Every row is validated, including
+  skipped tickets. Invalid rows or insufficient stock reject the entire file
+  with `bad_request` and a message naming the CSV row (header is row 1).
+  Consumption uses `soldAt` and ledger ref `sale:<ticket>`.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD`: returns an array of
+  `{ "itemId": 1, "theoretical": 0.6, "actual": 0.8, "variance": 0.2 }`,
+  sorted by item id. Dates are inclusive UTC days, with `from <= to`.
+  Theoretical use is the ingredient quantities saved with imported sales;
+  actual use includes every `consume` movement. Variance is actual minus
+  theoretical, in the item's unit. Items with neither use are omitted.
