+## Sales (schema 3)
+
+- Schema 2 migrates to schema 3 by adding an empty `sales` array and a `sale`
+  sequence. Existing data is preserved.
+- Each sales row stores an id, ticket, UTC `soldAt` instant, dishId, qty (whole
+  portions) and scaled `ingredients` (`itemId`, `qty`). Ingredient snapshots
+  preserve theoretical use when a recipe or dish changes later.
+- Tickets are unique across imports, but can have multiple rows in one import.
+  A previously imported ticket is skipped as a whole. A file commits all its
+  sales, batch changes, movements and sequence changes together or none.
